From 5405dabc43fd3767d5036b0e15f1c0a4f91c010a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project contributors <contributors@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:30:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-status: show CPU temperature and frequency on
 overview

Read the CPU package temperature from the coretemp/k10temp hwmon drivers,
falling back to thermal zones, and report the average current frequency from
the cpufreq sysfs files with a /proc/cpuinfo fallback. Append both rows to
the System status card after the load average.

Grant the status ACL read access to the required sysfs and procfs paths,
including the symlink-resolved hwmon and cpufreq policy paths. Sample the
frequency after the status poll burst settles so the dashboard does not
report the boost clock caused by its own refresh. Add zh_Hans translations
for the two new labels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/luci-base/po/templates/base.pot       |   8 +
 modules/luci-base/po/zh_Hans/base.po          |   8 +
 .../view/status/include/10_system.js          | 184 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-status-index.json     |  16 ++
 4 files changed, 214 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

